      "final_text": "Registration for Riley Fox (riley.fox@example.com) for 1 General admission ticket to the WebMCP Community Workshop was completed successfully.\n\nOrder details captured:\n- Order code (starts with o_): o_um79FJnUwfm9o\n- Displayed Order Reference: O-2VEX7NS\n- Attendee: Riley Fox, riley.fox@example.com\n- Ticket: General admission (1)\n- Order Date: Aug 20, 2026 3:44am GMT+3\n- Event: WebMCP Community Workshop\n\nHowever, I was unable to locate an 'order lookup' feature on the event page (http://127.0.0.1:3215/event/1/webmcp-community-workshop) despite extensive attempts: scrolling through the entire page (top to bottom), searching page text for 'order', 'lookup', 'find', 'already have', 'my order' (no relevant matches), extracting all links via JavaScript (only found organizer link, promo code link, and footer legal/Hi.Events links - no lookup link), and trying several direct URL guesses for a Hi.Events order-lookup/status page (/event/1/webmcp-community-workshop/order-lookup, /event/1/webmcp-community-workshop/order/o_um79FJnUwfm9o, /checkout/1/o_um79FJnUwfm9o) - all returned 404 Page Not Found. Clicking the ticket selection area again only reopened the ticket purchase form, not a lookup modal.\n\nAs a result, I could not complete the final step of using the order code and email to check and report the order's status through the site's lookup feature. The order info has been saved to order_info.md for reference. This part of the task remains incomplete given the site's UI did not expose a discoverable order lookup mechanism within my step budget.\n\nAttachments:\n\norder_info.md:\n# Registration Order Info\n\n- Attendee: Riley Fox\n- Email: riley.fox@example.com\n- Ticket: General admission (1)\n- Order code (starts with o_): o_um79FJnUwfm9o\n- Displayed Order Reference: O-2VEX7NS\n- Order Date: Aug 20, 2026 3:44am GMT+3\n- Event: WebMCP Community Workshop\n\n"
    },
